; The sample's scenarios: `--baker sim` runs each, from a fresh scene, for its seconds, and
; judges it by its objectives (objectives.dta). The game draws no random numbers, so every
; seed gives the same run.

; From standing, one jump held to its apex and back to the ground.
(scenario jump (desc "One held jump peaks at the data's jump height")
   (seconds 2)
   (at 0.5 {player.hold_jump})            ; settled on the floor first
   (objectives jump.apex))

; The same jump, against the level: the first platform's top is 100 px above the floor, the
; second's 180 px. A jump should clear the first with 10 px to spare, and the climb should
; take two jumps, so a jump from the floor stays at least 20 px below the second.
(scenario reach (desc "A jump from the floor clears the first platform, not the second")
   (seconds 2)
   (at 0.5 {player.hold_jump})
   (objectives reach.first_platform reach.not_second_platform))
